From f05748eada7716020ee6a8e4442b750a808d2703 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:37:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [Scheduler] Prefill lanes do not split aligned chunks to
 their shares

With aligned prefill chunks a chunk cannot be partial, so capping it at a
lane's share only skipped it: two long prompts each given half the
budget were skipped every step, kept their lanes, and nothing prefilled.
An aligned chunk now takes the step's budget when that holds it; lanes
still choose which prefills may run and rotate whole chunks. Unaligned
chunks keep their shares.
